    "answer": "Reviewed all available household sources and transaction records. No new fees, duplicate charges, refund promises, cancellation notices, or deadlines appeared. The household note lists account names but no support URLs.\n\n- **Peak Wireless:** Eight 2024 payments totaling $232.56 fall within the official program\u2019s date range. The official page says eligibility requires an unlimited data plan and lists an average $60 payment. I verified the claim site through that page. The existing eligibility question and attestation proposal are still pending, so the claim is blocked on the user\u2019s answer and decision. I scheduled a December 1 follow-up before the December 31 deadline.\n- **Peak email:** The $240 email came from an unrelated sender and asks for bank details through a different link. Treat it as unverified; don\u2019t use its link or share account details.\n- **Tidal Tickets:** Five payments total $65.30. The matched program is paying automatically, with no claim required. I found no matching payment in the available transaction history and saved a watch item; cash any check within 90 days.\n- **Other leads:** Spotify, rent, and Harborline Parking remain inventory only; the records don\u2019t show that Spotify is unwanted, rent is erroneous, or Harborline continued billing after February.\n\nThe review status is complete. No company request was submitted.",
